From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 09:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] locale/programs: use GCC fallthrough attribute for native
 helper build

`cross-localedef-native` is built with the host compiler. On this build host
that is GCC 9.5, which does not accept the C23-style `[[fallthrough]]`
attribute used in glibc 2.43's locale parser sources. The generated keyword
headers already contain GCC-version guards, but these two source files do not.

Use the GCC/Clang fallthrough attribute in the two affected switch sites so
the helper builds with older native compilers.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [native host compiler compatibility]
Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 locale/programs/charmap.c   | 4 ++--
 locale/programs/repertoire.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/locale/programs/charmap.c b/locale/programs/charmap.c
index d83d8fd..66a0d54 100644
--- a/locale/programs/charmap.c
+++ b/locale/programs/charmap.c
@@ -548,7 +548,7 @@ parse_charmap (struct linereader *cmfile, int verbose,
 	      state = 4;
 	      continue;
 	    }
-	  [[fallthrough]];
+	  __attribute__ ((__fallthrough__));
 
 	case 5:
 	  if (nowtok != tok_charcode)
@@ -712,7 +712,7 @@ parse_charmap (struct linereader *cmfile, int verbose,
 	      state = 95;
 	      continue;
 	    }
-	  [[fallthrough]];
+	  __attribute__ ((__fallthrough__));
 
 	case 96:
 	  if (nowtok != tok_number)
diff --git a/locale/programs/repertoire.c b/locale/programs/repertoire.c
index 9630a7e..3442912 100644
--- a/locale/programs/repertoire.c
+++ b/locale/programs/repertoire.c
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ repertoire_read (struct linereader *repfile, struct charset_t *charset,
 
 	  /* Otherwise we start reading the character definitions.  */
 	  state = 2;
-	  [[fallthrough]];
+	  __attribute__ ((__fallthrough__));
 
 	case 2:
 	  /* We are now are in the body.  Each line
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@ repertoire_read (struct linereader *repfile, struct charset_t *charset,
 	      state = 4;
 	      continue;
 	    }
-	  [[fallthrough]];
+	  __attribute__ ((__fallthrough__));
 
 	case 5:
 	  /* We expect a value of the form <Uxxxx> or <Uxxxxxxxx> where
-- 
2.43.0
